      "text": "Project\nSummary\nI built a small business \nnetwork in Cisco \nPacket Tracer using a \nCisco 2911 router and \nthree Cisco 2960 \nswitches. I configured \nthree separate IP \nnetworks, connected \nPCs, laptops, printers, \nand a server, and \nconfigured the router \ninterfaces to allow \ncommunication \nbetween the different \nsubnets. I then tested \nthe network using \nICMP traffic and \nPacket Tracer’s \nsimulation tools to \nverify connectivity and \ntroubleshoot the \nnetwork.\nP.5 - Architecture & Configuration\nProject Outcome\nThis project gave me hands on experience building a small business network from the \nground up in Cisco Packet Tracer. I worked with multiple network segments, switches, a \ncentral router, end-user devices, printers, and a dedicated server network.\nWorking through the project helped me better understand how IP addressing, routing, \nswitching, and network segmentation come together in a real network environment. I \nalso gained experience configuring Cisco devices, troubleshooting connectivity issues, \nand testing communication between different parts of the network.\n"
