      "image": "assets/windows-2.webp",
      "text": "Overview:\nThis Windows 11 Home system is set-up in Virtual-Box with virtual hardware and network configurations. \nBit-Locker Encryption is used for its 80GB of virtual storage to ensure data is safe, even at rest. DNS > \nHTTPS is enabled with Cloudflare as the primary DNS,  this improves the system security by encrypting \nDNS searches by sending them through HTTPS (443) blockinf ISP DNS snooping. Both RDP (3389) and \nSSH (22) has been disabled to prevent brute-force entry attempts to the system. Anti-malware software has \nbeen set up with BitDefender real-time protection and prevention. Overall this system now provides full data \nencryption, privacy improvements, and offline recovery and data security for the user.\nDefense In Depth:\n____________________________________________________________\nData:\n- BitLocker Full Disk Encryption | 80 GB Virtual | “Secures live and resting data on the device”\n- Offline Disk Encryption | 2-TB HDD | “For encrypted offline system backups”\n- Recovery Drive | “USB windows recovery drive for backup system recovery”\n- Encrypted File Backups | “Windows data backups [Folders, Apps, Settings, Credentials]”\n- Monthly Drive Optimization | “De-fragment drives to re-organize fragmented data and improve system \nperformance”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nApplication:\n- Daily Security & App Updates | “Ensures any new vulnerabilities in applications or systems are patched”\n- Protection From Non-Trusted Apps | “Keep non-trusted application permissions limited, only allowed if I \nallow it”\n- Removed Windows Bloatware | “Removed all unnecessary applications pre-installed with windows for \nimproved performance”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nHost:\n- Windows Backups (Disk Encrypted) | “Consistent backups for easy roll-backs”\n- Offline External Backups | “Resting encrypted backups on external HDD” \n- Disabled Root Log-In (UAC) | “Reduces attack surface of brute-force attacks to privileged” accounts”\n- Secure Boot | “Ensures the system boots from trusted sources only”\n- Bit-Defender Anti-Malware | “Real-Time malware protection and prevention”\n- BIOS Password | Bare Metal | “Keeps unauthorized users from accessing boot-loader options”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nNetwork:\n- Windows Defender Firewall | (Disabled Incoming) | “Stops other devices from attempting access to the \nsystem unless allowed”\n- Port 22 Disabled (SSH) | “Disabled when not in use to prevent brute-force attacks and possible lateral \nmovement”\n- Port 3389 Disabled (RDP) | “Disabled when not in use to prevent brute-force attacks”\n- Bit-Defender VPN | “Encrypts internet traffic and IP address”\n- DNS > HTTPS (DOH) (Cloud-Flare 1.0.0.1 – Google 8.8.8.8) | “Reduce DNS snooping and spoofing by \nencrypting DNS queries”\n________________________________________________________________________________\n| Created By https://B-Wynkoop.github.io For System Hardening |\n| GitHub | https://github.com/B-Wynkoop |\n| LinkedIn | https://www.linkedin.com/in/d-brady-wynkoop-0ba0a3379/ |\n"
