      "text": "Overview:\nThis Apple MacOS system is set up for everyday use with strict security measures in place. Full disk \nencryption with AES and multi-factor authentication procedures set for account and setting changes. This \nsystem is tailored to transition into security and pen-testing with virtualization. Application permissions and \nsignatures are currently verified by built in and pre-signed applications. Full browser hardening, encrypted \nDNS, rotating wi-fi address, VPN and more all help stay secure while connected to your home or other \nnetwork.\nDefense In Depth:\n____________________________________________________________\nData:\n- FileVault Disk Encryption | 256 GB | “XTS-AES-128 encrypted drive for at rest security”\n- TimeMachine Encrypted Backups | “Ensures roll back plans are in place in case of system breaks”\n- External Disk Encryption | 2-TB HDD | “Data integrity and security with encryption stored offline”\n- “Passwords” Credential Encryption | “Login credentials, notes, keys and more all encrypted” \n________________________________________________________________________________\nApplication:\n- Auto Security & App Updates | “Auto system and security updates to remove prior known vulnerabilities”\n- Removed Unused Applications | “Removed unused apps to lower the systems attack surface”\n- Browser Hardening | [4] Web: | “Security configurations for browsers to ensure sensitive data stays secure”\n- Disbaled Guest Account | “Deleting guest accounts help reduce breach points”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nHost:\n- Full System Backups (Encrypted) | “Time machine backups sent to an encrypted HDD then stored at rest \noffline”\n- System Integrity Protection | “Checks system files for file manipulation to enforce system integrity”\n- Secure Boot | “Apple Silicon sets this automatically, default denies boot loading any OS unsigned by \nApple”\n- Malware Scanner & Remover | XProtect (Re-mediator) | “Built in to Mac, XProtect scans for malware on \nthe device, if found XProtect re-mediator then removes the malware”\n- Blocked Unsigned Applications | GateKeeper | “Keeps untrusted apps from accessing sensitive or system \nfiles”\n- Lockdown mode | On/Off | “In case of a cyber attack, lockdown removes your connections from nearly \neverything removing access for the malicious actor”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nNetwork:\n- NordVPN | “Hides IP address and prevents ISP DNS snooping”\n- Rotating Private Wi-Fi Address | “Reduces tracking of the system locally and on other networks”\n- Stealth Mode | “Disables response to network pings”\n- Encrypted DNS (DoH) | “Cloudflare encrypted DNS > HTTPS”\n- MacOS Firewall | (Deny Incoming | Allow Outgoing) | “Reduce incoming data from unknown or untrusted \nsources”\n- Only Allowed Built-In and Signed Software | “Restricts unauthorized users from accessing privileged \npermissions”\n- Port 22 Disabled (SSH) | “Disables secure shell access to this machine”\n- Port 3389 Disabled (RDP) | “Disabled remote desktop access to the system”\n________________________________________________________________________________\n| Created By https://B-Wynkoop.github.io For System Hardening |\n| GitHub | https://github.com/B-Wynkoop |\n| LinkedIn | https://www.linkedin.com/in/d-brady-wynkoop-0ba0a3379/ |\n"
