      "text": "Overview:\nThis system is configured for everyday personal desktop use. Encryptions added at every layer as well as \ntwo-factor and multi-factor authentication methods implemented. A BIOS password is implemented and root \nlogin disabled to ensure unauthorized access to bootloaders or privileged permissions. Browser hardening \nwas also implemented with tracking, ad, malware, and secure DNS queries. Daily system, snap, and flatpak \nupdates to ensure up to date security patches. With NordVPN the systems IP address and network traffic is \nencrypted enforcing strict security policies. Malware detection and removal tools, root and bootkit scanners, \nand system audits for hardening all set up for peace of mind when using this system.\nDefense In Depth:\n____________________________________________________________\nData:\n- Internal Disk Encryption | (2) 1-TB SSD | “Data secured at rest”\n- External Disk Encryption | 2-TB HDD | “Offline data backups secured at rest”\n- External USB Encryption | 256-GB | “Encrypted USB for extra storage”\n- Encrypted File Backups (Monthly) | “Backups to external HDD stored offline”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nApplication:\n- Daily System & App Updates | “Patches known vulnerabilities in systems and applications”\n- App Armour | “Keeps app privileges to a minimum”\n- FireJail | “Sandboxes any application the user desires”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nHost:\n- TimeShift (Encrypted Recovery Snapshots Daily) | “Snapshots taken (2) hourly, (2) daily, and (2) monthly” \n- Disabled Root Log-In | “Lower the risk of root access to the system”\n- Brute Force Prevention | Fail2Ban | “Monitors log files for multiple login attempts, then blocks the IP”\n- BIOS Password | “Prevents boot loader and BIOS tampering”\n- Suricata IDS & IPS | “Monitors network traffic for suspicious behavior and blocks it”\n__________________________