      "image": "assets/kali-2.webp",
      "text": "Overview:\nThis system is set-up in Virtual-Box with virtual hardware and network configurations. This Kali-Linux \nconfiguration is intended to run a variety of penetration testing tools securely.  Full disk encryption with \nLUKS as well as system backups and scheduled snapshots. FireJail is set up on this machine so that \napplications can be sandboxed for further permission managing. All system package updates use Cloudflare \nserver instead of community for fast and reliable package updates. Antivirus and secure boot are disabled to \nallow Kali’s penetration tools to run effectively and efficiently. This systems security is configured for \npenetration testing as intended with Kali-Linux, additional security has been added to the users system as an \nextra layer of defense when working with malicious data.\nDefense In Depth:\n____________________________________________________________\nData:\n- LUKS Disk Encryption | 60 GB Virtual | “60GB of LUKS encrypted virtual memory”\n- External Disk Encryption | 2-TB HDD | “External encrypted 2TB HDD, stays offline”\n- Encrypted Timeshift Backups | “(2) Timeshift snapshots hourly, (2) Daily, and (1) monthly all saved to its \nown partition in the virtual drive”  \n- Clonezilla Full System Backups | “A live boot USB allowing a full system backup offline” \n- BitWarden Account Encryption | “Encrypted password, key, and note manager for accounts”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nApplication:\n- Daily Security & App Updates | “Terminal full upgrades for apt managed packages (kali tools, etc)”\n- FireJail (Sandbox) | “Keeps applications sandboxed to help control system access”\n________________________________________________________________________________\nHost:\n- Full System Backups (Encrypted) | “Without the passphrase all backed up data is unreadable”\n- Disabled Root Log-In | “Keeps unauthorized users from accessing a higher privileged account”\n- Secure Boot | “Secure boot is deactivated to prevent problems with booting as Kali’s kernel at default is \nmissing those signed keys”\n- Antivirus | “Any anti-malware or virus software is not installed on this machine as this system is \nintentionally used for pen-testing, any malware or virus prevention can remove some abilities to run kali \ntools”\n- BIOS Password | Bare Metal | “Prevents manipulation with the boot-loader and BIOS settings”\n- File History of 7 days – Trash & Temporary Files Delete after 7 days | “File history and trash that could \nhave sensitive information get removed after 7 days, cleans any temp files as well” \n________________________________________________________________________________\nNetwork:\n- NordVPN | “Hides IP and encrypts your traffic,  also prevents ISP DNS snooping”\n- UFW | (Deny Incoming | Allow Outgoing) | “Uncomplicated Firewall used for simple !incoming =outgoing \nand port rules”\n- Restrict Ports < 1024 for Privileged Users | “Restricts any port < 1024 for access only by root”\n- Port 22 Disabled (SSH) | “Disabled secure shell access to the system through port 22”\n- Port 3389 Disabled (RDP) | “Disabled remote desktop access through port 3389”\nKali Tweaks:\n- Package Mirror Cloudflare CDN | “Uses Cloudflare networks to update packages for reliable and secure \ndownloads”\n- HTTPS Protocol | “Defaults to using the secure version of hypertext transfer protocol”\n- Disabled Samba Client | “Disabled the system from accessing windows file sharing until needed”\n________________________________________________________________________________\n"
